SUMMARY:Cane Creek Mountain Natural Area
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nWe will hike the NEWER tra
 ils (as well as one old trail) at the Cain Creek Mountain Natural Area. We
  will meet at the PEACH ORCHARD TAILHEAD and hike the Varnals Creek\, Moun
 tain View\, Lark\, and Pioneer Camp trails for a total of 8.25 miles.\nhtt
 ps://www.alamancecountync.gov/community/parks_recreation/cane_creek_mounta
 ins_natural_area_location_hours_rules.php\n\nThe pace will be 2.8-3 miles 
 per hour. It is hilly but well maintained and no major steam crossings.\n\
 nIf there is a good chance of HEAVY RAIN I will cancel by 7am on Monday. L
 ight drizzle will not hold me back.\n\nBy participating in this event\, yo
 u agree to the terms below:\n\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I full
 y realize that this activity involves a risk of personal injury\, property
  damage\, or loss of my person or property. I hereby for myself\, my heirs
 \, executors and administrators\, and same for persons with whom are in my
  party\, waive and release any claims or rights against Triangle Hiking & 
 Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of its owners and coordinators for any and all
  injury\, damages or loss to my person or property incurred during this ac
 tivity. I also understand that THOG organizers are not required\, nor shou
 ld it be assumed that they are CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified
  and I am responsible for my own personal safety.
